## 1. Purpose and Scope

The MedSync Health Fleet Policy establishes guidelines for the acquisition, assignment, use, maintenance, and disposal of all company-owned or leased vehicles globally. The policy ensures compliance with local regulations, promotes employee safety, and supports the company's commitment to operational efficiency and sustainability.

This policy applies to all MedSync Health employees who are assigned a company vehicle or receive a vehicle allowance as part of their compensation package. The policy is managed by the Operations Department, which oversees the support for our **1,200 employees** across four global offices [1].

## 2. Fleet Management and Oversight

The overall management of the company fleet is the responsibility of the Operations Department, led by the Chief Operating Officer (COO), James Thompson. The Operations team, which comprises **120 employees**, is responsible for procurement, maintenance scheduling, insurance, and compliance monitoring.

### 2.1. Fleet Profile

MedSync Health maintains a small, specialized fleet of vehicles primarily for the Sales, Customer Success, and Executive teams who require regular travel to support our **520 hospital and 3,200 clinic customers** [1]. The fleet is distributed across our primary operational regions:

| Office Location | Employee Headcount | Primary Fleet Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Boston, MA (HQ)** | 650 | Executive & North America Sales Support |
| **London, UK** | 280 | EMEA Sales & Customer Success |
| **Berlin, Germany** | 150 | EMEA Sales & Customer Success |
| **Singapore** | 120 | APAC Sales & Customer Success |

## 3. Vehicle Allocation and Eligibility

### 3.1. Eligibility Criteria

Company vehicles are allocated based on job function and demonstrated business need. Eligible roles typically include:
*   C-Level Executives and Vice Presidents.
*   Regional Sales Directors and Managers.
*   Customer Success Managers with a territory requiring frequent travel (e.g., 50% or more of working time).
*   Select Operations and IT personnel requiring on-site support for critical infrastructure (See **OPS-003: IT Infrastructure** for details on server and network maintenance).

### 3.2. Vehicle Tiers and Budget

To ensure fiscal responsibility and consistency across regions, MedSync Health utilizes a tiered vehicle system with maximum monthly lease costs denominated in **AED** (United Arab Emirates Dirham), the company's designated internal financial currency.

| Vehicle Tier | Eligible Roles | Maximum Monthly Lease/Allowance (AED) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Tier 1 (Executive)** | C-Level, VPs | AED 8,000 |
| **Tier 2 (Field/Sales)** | Directors, Managers, CSMs | AED 5,500 |

The total annual budget allocated for fleet leasing, maintenance, and insurance is **AED 3,500,000**, which is managed within the Operations Department's overall budget of **AED 44,160,000** [1].

## 4. Vehicle Usage and Conduct

### 4.1. Permitted Use

Company vehicles are provided primarily for business use. Limited personal use is permitted, provided it does not interfere with business needs and is in compliance with local tax regulations. Employees must adhere to all traffic laws and regulations in the jurisdiction where the vehicle is operated. Any violation may result in disciplinary action (See **HR-001: Employee Conduct Policy**).

### 4.2. Maintenance and Repair

Employees are responsible for scheduling routine maintenance (e.g., oil changes, tire rotation) as required by the manufacturer. All maintenance and repair costs must be pre-approved by the Operations Department, with all invoices processed in **AED** for central accounting purposes.

## 5. Sustainability and Environmental Commitment

MedSync Health is committed to reducing its environmental footprint, aligning with the requirements outlined in **OPS-010: Corporate Sustainability Policy** and **OPS-011: Carbon Footprint Reporting**.

### 5.1. Low-Emission Mandate

All new vehicle acquisitions or lease renewals must prioritize low-emission or fully electric vehicles (EVs) where feasible and cost-effective within the allocated budget (AED 5,500 - AED 8,000 monthly range). The Operations Department aims for a minimum of **60% of the global fleet** to be electric or hybrid by the end of FY 2027.

### 5.2. Telematics and Data

All company vehicles are equipped with GPS and telematics systems for safety, efficiency, and compliance monitoring. This data is used to optimize routes, monitor vehicle health, and calculate carbon emissions for reporting under OPS-011. The IT Infrastructure team (referenced in OPS-003) maintains the security and privacy of this data.

---

## 6. Policy Violations and Disciplinary Action

Any misuse of a company vehicle, failure to maintain the vehicle, or repeated traffic violations will be subject to disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment and revocation of the company vehicle privilege. Details on disciplinary procedures are outlined in **HR-001: Employee Conduct Policy**.

